# Context

## Background
The repo previously documented only manual archive installs and source builds, which left the curl-install path implicit and forced users to assemble the release workflow themselves.

## Why This Way
Added a small POSIX installer that downloads the matching GitHub Release archive, verifies SHA256SUMS, installs into ~/.local/bin by default, and avoids mutating shell startup files. Release publishing now emits pinned installer assets so a script fetched from a tagged release installs that tagged version by default, while the GitHub Pages URL can still track the latest release.

## Gotchas
The docs site URL and the release asset URL intentionally have different version semantics. docs/README.md had unrelated local edits, so it was left out of this commit.

